From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:16:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/20] qwen3_5: a windowed layer's mHC routers load with their
 shapes checked

The HIP loader reads the two fp32 routers every mHC layer carries
(mhc_attn and mhc_ffn, [outputs, streams * hidden] weights with an
[outputs] bias each) for the layers the config's window holds, refuses
one whose shape disagrees with the streams it declares, and carries
them through the device model, the bridge and the forward's view. A
layer outside the window, or a model without mHC, loads as before;
the synthetic dense checkpoint gains a looped variant that exercises
the read end to end.
